WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.630
Inherited will...

3
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.540
the tides of time,
and humanity's dreams...

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.370
They cannot be stopped.

5
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.480
As long as people seek freedom,

6
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.110
these things will never cease to be.

7
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.920
<b>Alubarna Palace</b>

8
00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.170
T-Terrible news, Commander Chaka!

9
00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.920
It's His Majesty!

10
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.550
What?! What are you saying?!

11
00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.220
He vanished!

12
00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:04.900
<b>Rebellion</b>

13
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.300
That's absurd!
Have you searched everywhere?!

14
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.370
Yes! Not only the palace, 
but the gardens and storehouses as well!

15
00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.520
Did he leave in 
the middle of the night?

16
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.010
Not possible.
The king's security is top-notch;

17
00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.350
nothing escapes our eyes!

18
00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.730
Then... Then, why?

19
00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:19.490
Why would the king be absent 
at the cusp of battle?!

20
00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.760
Find him! Search beyond 
the palace walls and in the towns!

21
00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:23.240
Yes, sir!

22
00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.560
Pell excels in finding people,

23
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.630
but unfortunately he's busy 
scouting out Rainbase.

24
00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:37.040
What has happened to His Majesty?

25
00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.570
I can't afford to act recklessly...

26
00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.100
Damn it!

27
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.220
Terrible news, Commander Chaka! 
It's His Majesty!

28
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.240
What is it?! 
Did you find him?!

29
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.830
Yes, sir! It seems he's in Nanohana. 
This information is reliable.

30
00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.470
I see! That's a relief!

31
00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.570
But... But... 
Unbelievably enough...

32
00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.030
C-Come again?!

33
00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.640
Koza!

34
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.990
Wait!
We're coming too!

35
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.330
Why now, all of a sudden?!

36
00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.300
How much farther can he fall?!

37
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.670
Don't hold to suspicion, Koza.

38
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.170
Why would he act 
so nonsensically?!

39
00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:27.140
You know His Majesty's
character very well.

40
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.640
All you old people say that.

41
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:36.650
I didn't follow you here to
Yuba for the king's sake.

42
00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.640
The Rebel Army is over
100,000 strong now!

43
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.870
Yeah, I heard.

44
00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:48.080
Apparently there've been casualties, too...

45
00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.260
It's nothing.

46
00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:02.980
A little rain ought to clear away 
his strange suspicions. Yes...

47
00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.840
What on earth?!

48
00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.610
The canal's been destroyed!

49
00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:09.010
Who would do this?!

50
00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:12.020
Now the water won't 
make it into town!

51
00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:18.360
It hasn't rained 
for over a year now!

52
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.180
Erumalu is done for!

53
00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.410
Don't hold to suspicion, Koza...

54
00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:34.500
I don't want to suspect you,
but people are dying of thirst!

55
00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.690
You may not be using it,
but you do have it!

56
00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:44.070
No. Wait for natural rain.
Dance powder summons misfortune.

57
00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.480
Just a little won't hurt anything!

58
00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:49.860
Even the smallest amount 
of rain might end the rebellion!

59
00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.680
Its use would only cascade into calamity.

60
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.650
Using it isn't so easy 
an undertaking, Koza.

61
00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.530
I can't just sit by... and watch 
as our towns dry up anymore!

62
00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:11.160
All this time, and you 
have not changed a bit.

63
00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.730
I have changed.

64
00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:15.870
I can fight.

65
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.750
I'm... going to...

66
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:25.720
I'm going to come here... 
and I'll take your rain!

67
00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.440
<b>Nanohana</b>

68
00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.610
Y-Your Majesty?

69
00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.440
What did you just say?

70
00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:43.050
Just as you heard.
I am honestly apologizing.

71
00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:49.060
It was I, Cobra, the king of Arabasta,
who stole this country's rain!

72
00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.650
Your Majesty Cobra... 
This is a joke, right?

73
00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.500
It has to be...

74
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.210
It is no joke.

75
00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.880
This is crazy...

76
00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.120
You only helped yourself 
when you know how we suffer?!

77
00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.880
That's far too selfish, 
even for you, sire!

78
00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:10.590
How dare you, a mere cretin, 
talk back to me, the king?

79
00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:16.400
I've come to Nanohana to
apologize for what I've done.

80
00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.810
What more do you want?

81
00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.650
My brother died in Yuba, you know...

82
00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:29.350
There is another reason I came 
all the way out to this city.

83
00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:34.840
As you know, dance powder is
outlawed by the World Government.

84
00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.090
If the outside world 
learns of its use,

85
00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:40.730
Navy Headquarters will take
action and destroy our country.

86
00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.570
This must be avoided.

87
00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:44.600
However, please remember;

88
00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:47.670
we found large batches of dance powder

89
00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.530
being smuggled into this town two years ago.

90
00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:54.390
It is necessary to eliminate 
all traces of that incident.

91
00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.140
You understand, do you not?

92
00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.310
You don't mean...

93
00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:02.790
That's right! If we are to be rid
of that terrible incident forever,

94
00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.770
we must be rid of this city and all of you!

95
00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.640
Wh-What?!

96
00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.890
That's insane!

97
00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.660
You're ordering us to die?!

98
00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.830
Hey! King!

99
00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.570
So it was all your fault!

100
00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:18.290
It's...

101
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:20.030
It's...

102
00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.670
It's because of you...

103
00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.130
You steal the rain and make 
all the towns dry up, you jerk!

104
00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.770
I'm gonna get you back 
for everyone...!

105
00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.430
Don't!

106
00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:42.310
Sire...

107
00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.980
Men! Burn Nanohana to the ground!

108
00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.740
Yes, sire!

109
00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:56.280
Koza!

110
00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:03.370
Koza. It's been a while.

111
00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.170
What the hell... 
do you think you're doing?

112
00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.150
Hey, King!

113
00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.150
Stop!

114
00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.820
I came to apologize, 
as you can see.

115
00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:14.650
Quit screwing around! 
Shut up!

116
00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:18.510
Do you realize what you're saying?!
How insulting this is?!

117
00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:22.020
I am the one who's been
using dance powder to–

118
00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.850
I said shut up!

119
00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.690
Why are you so angry?

120
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:26.690
Koza...

121
00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.540
Surely even you can appreciate...

122
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.540
Sire...

123
00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:30.440
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

124
00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.090
...that I...

125
00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.090
You asshole!

126
00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:35.910
Do you know how the people felt

127
00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:38.860
as they died off in dried-up towns?!

128
00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.710
They never succumbed 
to malice or anger for you!

129
00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.270
"It isn't the king's fault"!

130
00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:44.630
"He's a great person"!

131
00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.650
Ever faithful, that's what they said, 
even as they lay there dying.

132
00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:52.340
At least have the decency
to keep lying about your innocence!

133
00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:56.840
How are they supposed to feel about this?!

134
00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.680
Koza!

135
00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.480
Leader!

136
00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:09.650
Koza!

137
00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:15.610
Well, I guess it's time!

138
00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:20.770
Didn't... Didn't we fight because...

139
00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:24.470
the kingdom...
no, everyone...

140
00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:27.920
wanted to know that answer?!

141
00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.200
At the very least...

142
00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.140
that's why I fought...

143
00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.110
You can't be serious!

144
00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.790
Here they come!

145
00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:08.000
A giant ship is about to crash! Run!

146
00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:15.010
What is that ship?!

147
00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.440
Mommy!

148
00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:35.480
I-It's toppling over!

149
00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:46.180
For a final operation, 
we barely lifted a finger.

150
00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.290
Have any of our assignments
ever been a challenge to us?

151
00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:54.920
That's a wrap!

152
00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.240
Now, light the fires 
so we can skedaddle!

153
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.500
Yes, sir!

154
00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.780
I just can't feel relaxed 
without this on!

155
00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:07.370
Koza! Say something! 
Koza! Hey!

156
00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.150
The Royal Army disappeared!

157
00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.150
What?!

158
00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:17.770
How deux you
like my kingliness?!

159
00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.950
That was great, 
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

160
00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:24.570
Put out the fires!

161
00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:27.540
The damn Royal Army lit fires and ran off!

162
00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.540
Hurry!

163
00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.080
Put out the fires!

164
00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:33.540
Now to meet up 
with Mr. 2 outside town.

165
00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.650
Alubarna's the finale.

166
00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:37.800
Hm.

167
00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:40.920
I look forward to it.

168
00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.780
Iffy! My favorite word is "iffy"!

169
00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:48.690
Because now it's iffy
whether the king remains king!

170
00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.570
The operation's a success!

171
00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.140
Where's Bunchi?!

172
00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:55.770
He's to the west of town, 
Mr. 2 Bon Kurei!

173
00:11:55.770 --> 00:12:00.650
Huh? The king turned
into a weird ballerina...

174
00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:02.810
It's no use! It won't go out!

175
00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.160
Damn the king!

176
00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.620
He was a fake!

177
00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:10.850
This is bad! 
Everyone's being tricked!

178
00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:12.960
I have to hurry and tell 'em!

179
00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.860
What a naughty little boy.
What do you think he's discovered?

180
00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.670
That imbecile was 
careless and slipped up.

181
00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:24.340
Who're you?!

182
00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.310
I take it there's no use 
in asking you to stay quiet.

183
00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.440
Water! We need more water!

184
00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:33.140
Wait! That's for my shop!
Can you pay for it?!

185
00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:35.640
Not now, you idiot! The town is on fire!

186
00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:36.670
Put out the fires!

187
00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:37.920
Water!

188
00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:41.260
It's no use. We can't
outpace the fire...

189
00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.100
We should probably run for it.

190
00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:49.080
Hang in there, Koza!
You're not the type to die like this!

191
00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.760
Hey! Take Koza!

192
00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.630
Little boy! Say something!

193
00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:02.590
This is terrible! 
Not even children are safe!

194
00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:04.250
I-It's not...

195
00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:07.010
What's that?! I'll stop
the bleeding! Don't talk!

196
00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.180
It's not what you think!
Everyone's being tricked!

197
00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.810
Hang in there, kid!

198
00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.100
Koza!

199
00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.340
This country...

200
00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:19.770
Let's end it.

201
00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:27.110
Contact all of our branches!
This will be our final battle!

202
00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:31.160
O-Okay, but we don't
have nearly enough weapons!

203
00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:33.960
No, we do now.

204
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:38.920
That ship that just crashed?
It was a seafaring armory.

205
00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:40.140
Seriously?!

206
00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.500
Yeah! It was full of weapons!

207
00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.680
It's almost like... divine providence.

208
00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.930
Oh, yeah? Some pipsqueak
spotted me? Swan-swan!

209
00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:59.090
Goodness... Now Mr. 4's team
just needs to do its thing.

210
00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:02.070
Fatty and the old hag 
know how to get things done!

211
00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:06.700
Kidnapping the king
will be a walk in the park for them!

212
00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:10.530
Hear me, Rebel Army!

213
00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.610
The Arabasta of old is long dead!

214
00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:18.610
This is the final battle!
We're going to capture Alubarna!

215
00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.730
We're going to launch an all-out assault!

216
00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:24.610
The king must pay!

217
00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:28.470
We'll build a new country!

218
00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.300
<b>Meanwhile, at Alubarna Palace</b>

219
00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:32.300
Nonsense!

220
00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.280
His Majesty Cobra would never do such a thing!

221
00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:36.640
It must be a mistake!

222
00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.620
But...

223
00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.350
his disappearance and 
subsequent arrival line up!

224
00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.460
He no longer has an alibi!

225
00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.190
All of Arabasta knows of

226
00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:49.300
the Nanohana incident, 
moving rebels everywhere to action!

227
00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.450
And what's more...

228
00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.240
the citizens' faith in His Majesty
has turned to hatred;

229
00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.900
they're now arming themselves.

230
00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.240
Their numbers are unknown!

231
00:14:56.240 --> 00:14:59.670
The entire country is enraged 
and headed for Alubarna.

232
00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:02.750
And now... 
there's no stopping this.

233
00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:12.340
Please, make your decision!
We will obey you!

234
00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:16.540
How can this be?!

235
00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:20.490
Even the king's words 
from yesterday are blurred now!

236
00:15:20.490 --> 00:15:23.560
In what do I put my trust?!

237
00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:29.290
Very well! We need only
fulfill our given duties!

238
00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.660
We are the Kingdom of Arabasta's 
royal guards!

239
00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:37.710
No country should crumble
in the absence of its king!

240
00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:41.080
Protect the truth you see before you!
Protect this country!

241
00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:43.290
Counter the Rebel Army!

242
00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:51.720
<b>Rainbase</b>

243
00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.140
What a horrifying plan...

244
00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.340
Well? Do you like it?

245
00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:08.310
The operation you once
participated in has now blossomed.

246
00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:13.040
If you listen closely, you can
probably hear the howls of Arabasta.

247
00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:15.860
They're all thinking the same thing:

248
00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.660
"Protect Arabasta."

249
00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:24.300
"Protect Arabasta. Protect Arabas–"

250
00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.290
Stop it!

251
00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.460
How can you be so cruel?!

252
00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.850
Isn't it just heartrending?

253
00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:37.300
Love for this country
is what will lead to its destruction.

254
00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.980
Is he stupid?

255
00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.240
Or did he not 
hear what I said?

256
00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:56.760
He's definitely stupid. But...

257
00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.120
that's also why he's our captain.

258
00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:05.420
I've made so many moves 
to make it as far as I have:

259
00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.430
the sabotage to instigate the citizens;

260
00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:11.090
directing the Royal Army's 
misconduct...

261
00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:17.420
Have you any idea why I'd go to
such lengths to attain this country?

262
00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:20.140
There's no deciphering 
what's in your desiccated head!

263
00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:24.180
Your tongue is 
as sharp as ever, Princess.

264
00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:29.650
Vivi!

265
00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:33.830
Now, now. What are you
trying to do, Miss Wednesday?

266
00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:35.530
Stop you!

267
00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:38.480
I'm going to stop you! 
There's still time!

268
00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:41.730
If I can just get to Alubarna east of here...

269
00:17:41.730 --> 00:17:44.910
If I can get there 
before the Rebel Army,

270
00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:47.000
I may be able to stop them!

271
00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.670
I absolutely refuse...

272
00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.970
to let you have your way!

273
00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:58.340
Vivi!

274
00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:04.770
The Rebel Army is 
quickly approaching!

275
00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.440
Listen! We must protect
Arabasta with our own hands!

276
00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:13.230
Sacrifice is met with bravery!
Face your foe with all your might!

277
00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:19.780
Counter the Rebel Army!
Get in position to intercept!

278
00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.500
Topple Alubarna!

279
00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.370
Are you okay, Koza?

280
00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.130
This is nothing!

281
00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.690
At this pace, we'll reach
Alubarna by morning!

282
00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.870
Keep up our march 
at this speed!

283
00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:43.470
Right!

284
00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.730
The decisive battle... 
will be at dawn!

285
00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.070
What a coincidence.

286
00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:59.420
We're just about 
to head to Alubarna too.

287
00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.780
If you'd like to come with us, then do so.

288
00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.870
Or...

289
00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:08.910
would you rather save these people?

290
00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:10.620
That's–

291
00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:15.360
The key to this cell?! 
Give it here!

292
00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:37.980
A hole?!

293
00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:53.210
It won't be too long before
their fight to the death begins.

294
00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:56.050
Even if you hurried to Alubarna from here,

295
00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.170
who knows if you'd 
make it in time?

296
00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.920
To stop the rebellion,

297
00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.610
you'd need to leave at once, 
Miss Wednesday.

298
00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:06.640
Or will you save these people instead?

299
00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.260
Although,

300
00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:12.390
I just inconveniently 
dropped the key below the floor...

301
00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:15.730
and into the bananagators' den.

302
00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.660
A bananagator!

303
00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:22.400
Bananagator?

304
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.490
Whoa! What's that?!

305
00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:26.870
An alligator's growing 
from that banana!

306
00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.400
Wh-What is that 
insanely huge alligator?!

307
00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:32.430
This room is underwater?!

308
00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:33.770
What a weird banana!

309
00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:35.690
You idiot! Look closer!

310
00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:39.340
It's an alligator with a banana
growing out of it! It's a weird gator!

311
00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.800
Hey...! What happened, Vivi?!

312
00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.830
A bananagator swallowed
the key to your cell!

313
00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.330
What?! Go and make it 
spit it out!

314
00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.110
That would be impossible!

315
00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:57.520
Bananagators are so ferocious

316
00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.270
that they even prey on sea kings!

317
00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.880
Get near one, 
and they eat you in one bite!

318
00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:07.140
I apologize for clumsily 
dropping the key.

319
00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:11.580
Plus, there's no telling
which one swallowed it.

320
00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:13.710
What?!

321
00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:15.450
I can't believe this guy!

322
00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.920
Damn! If we could just get out of here,

323
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.310
I'd gut those reptiles!

324
00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.670
You're so dumb, Zoro!

325
00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.240
We can't get out because 
the key got eaten!

326
00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:25.220
I know that!

327
00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.180
Well, then.

328
00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:33.140
We must be going 
a little earlier than you.

329
00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.390
Also, this room 
will automatically

330
00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.350
get wiped out 
in one hour's time.

331
00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:41.570
This secret underground room 
I once used

332
00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:44.800
as Baroque Works' president 
is no longer necessary.

333
00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:49.820
It will soon fill with water and
be submerged in Rainbase's lake.

334
00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.740
One million innocent citizens,

335
00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.490
or a mere four pirates 
with no future?

336
00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:57.290
You must choose who to save,

337
00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:00.770
though the odds are low for both.

338
00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:05.550
Your feelings are your ante, 
Miss Wednesday.

339
00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.720
Do you enjoy gambling?

340
00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:15.810
The fools living in this country 
made this job so much easier.

341
00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:21.500
The juvenile rebels and the old man
digging in Yuba, for example.

342
00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:24.530
Wh-What?! You mean the dry old guy?!

343
00:22:28.050 --> 00:22:32.840
A foolish old man who keeps
pecking away every day

344
00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:36.000
at an oasis that's long dead.

345
00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:40.060
So many sandstorms come his way, 
yet he just keeps at it.

346
00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:43.410
Why, you...!

347
00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:45.330
Tell me, Straw Hat Luffy.

348
00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:47.430
Isn't it odd that sandstorms

349
00:22:47.430 --> 00:22:51.510
keep hitting the same towns 
so precisely, time after time?

350
00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:02.810
What are you saying?

351
00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:16.700
Yuba, you see...

352
00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:22.830
can't be beaten by
some lousy sandstorms!

353
00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:26.000
I'll dig it back up as
many times as it takes!

354
00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:28.670
As many times as it takes!

355
00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:32.110
As many times as it takes...

356
00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:34.470
You're the one... 
who caused it?!

357
00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:42.900
Vivi-chan.

358
00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:46.450
I have faith in His Majesty!

359
00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:49.900
His character makes him incapable 
of betraying his own country.

360
00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:53.360
I-I'll kill you!

361
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:04.580
Water's leaking in!

362
00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:09.030
The whole room's gonna be
flooded before too long!

363
00:24:09.030 --> 00:24:11.740
Vivi! Help! Do something!

364
00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:14.140
I don't want only 
one hour to live!

365
00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:15.510
Quit freaking out.

366
00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:19.080
Really, Zoro?! How can I not freak out at a time like this?!

367
00:24:19.080 --> 00:24:20.270
We'll die if we just sit here!

368
00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:22.830
Don't you understand?!

369
00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:26.370
The country... 
or my friends, you say?!

370
00:24:26.370 --> 00:24:29.500
I doubt you really plan
on giving anything back!

371
00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:34.030
You plan to take my life, too,
before I reach Alubarna!

372
00:24:34.360 --> 00:24:36.030
I know full well...

373
00:24:36.030 --> 00:24:40.500
that nothing will end 
unless I beat you!

374
00:24:41.350 --> 00:24:43.460
You don't know the first thing...

375
00:24:44.090 --> 00:24:49.380
about this country's people,
history, way of life...

376
00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:51.300
You don't know 
anything about it!

377
00:25:11.390 --> 00:25:12.880
Vivi!

378
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:16.350
Do something! 
Get us out of here!

379
00:25:16.350 --> 00:25:18.370
Luffy...

380
00:25:19.250 --> 00:25:22.500
Finally starting to beg 
for your life, Straw Hat Luffy?

381
00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:27.340
But it's only natural.
Everyone is afraid of dying.

382
00:25:27.340 --> 00:25:28.960
If we...

383
00:25:29.590 --> 00:25:32.760
If we die, then who's 
gonna kick your ass?!

384
00:25:39.470 --> 00:25:42.180
Don't flatter yourself, 
small-timer.

385
00:25:42.730 --> 00:25:44.640
You're the "small-timer"!

386
00:25:49.650 --> 00:25:54.010
Well, this is your chance to
abandon them, Miss Wednesday.

387
00:25:54.010 --> 00:25:56.070
If you wish to stop the rebellion, that is.

388
00:26:06.130 --> 00:26:08.920
It's... so big!

389
00:26:09.350 --> 00:26:11.350
Alright! Beat it, Vivi!

390
00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:13.920
That's crazy talk! 
It's too huge!

391
00:26:13.920 --> 00:26:17.530
Vivi! Run! You can't 
beat it! But help us!

392
00:26:17.530 --> 00:26:19.310
You're the one 
who's talking crazy!

393
00:26:19.310 --> 00:26:22.010
Wait! Look out the windows!

394
00:26:22.550 --> 00:26:24.440
They're all waiting 
for their turn!

395
00:26:24.440 --> 00:26:26.140
They see us as food!

396
00:26:26.140 --> 00:26:29.980
We're all gonna be in their
stomachs in an hour?!

397
00:26:33.660 --> 00:26:35.480
Peacock Str–

398
00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:39.660
I-It's fast!

399
00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:41.950
That chomp made quick work 
of those stairs!

400
00:26:41.950 --> 00:26:43.530
What a jaw!

401
00:26:46.540 --> 00:26:48.070
Vivi!

402
00:26:48.070 --> 00:26:52.650
Damn! These monsters 
are unstoppable!

403
00:26:52.650 --> 00:26:54.210
Ow...

404
00:26:54.220 --> 00:26:57.720
Vivi! Run!

405
00:26:56.040 --> 00:26:57.720
Get up!

406
00:26:57.720 --> 00:27:00.640
Vivi! It's gonna eat you!

407
00:27:08.950 --> 00:27:12.020
Someone's calling.

408
00:27:12.670 --> 00:27:14.190
What?

409
00:27:14.950 --> 00:27:17.110
Hello? Hello?

410
00:27:17.550 --> 00:27:18.550
Can you hear me?

411
00:27:18.550 --> 00:27:20.980
Yes, I hear you. 
From the millions, right?

412
00:27:20.980 --> 00:27:23.070
Hey, does this thing work?

413
00:27:23.070 --> 00:27:25.790
I've never used a 
baby transponder snail before.

414
00:27:25.790 --> 00:27:29.120
Yes, everything is fine.
You can talk just as you are.

415
00:27:29.910 --> 00:27:31.710
What do you want?

416
00:27:30.670 --> 00:27:31.710
Huh?

417
00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:33.960
Just spit out your report! 
What happened?

418
00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:37.250
Oh, I've heard 
that voice before.

419
00:27:37.250 --> 00:27:38.920
Hm?

420
00:27:39.710 --> 00:27:42.510
Hey there!
You've reached The Shit Shack.

421
00:27:43.330 --> 00:27:45.340
The Shit Shack?

422
00:27:45.990 --> 00:27:52.040
Oh? It sounds like 
you remember me. Fantastic.

423
00:27:52.040 --> 00:27:54.950
Hey there!
You've reached The Shit Shack.

424
00:27:54.950 --> 00:27:56.460
Making a reservation?

425
00:27:56.460 --> 00:27:58.920
Quit fooling around, you idiot.

426
00:27:58.920 --> 00:28:01.800
Transponder snail?
Wh-What do you mean?

427
00:28:01.800 --> 00:28:04.990
I never used a transponder snail
while on Little Garden.

428
00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:10.960
I'm certain we have all four
Straw Hat pirates inside that cell.

429
00:28:12.310 --> 00:28:14.900
All that's left is their pet.

430
00:28:14.900 --> 00:28:17.420
Does this mean 
there are still others?

431
00:28:17.420 --> 00:28:18.680
Hey, did you hear that?

432
00:28:18.680 --> 00:28:20.320
"The Shit Shack?" Could it be...?

433
00:28:20.320 --> 00:28:22.090
San–

434
00:28:20.920 --> 00:28:22.090
Wait, Luffy!

435
00:28:22.090 --> 00:28:24.660
The enemy doesn't 
know about him!

436
00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:29.640
He was in his room when Mr. 2 
showed up, so they never met!

437
00:28:30.150 --> 00:28:31.210
Sanji...

438
00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:34.710
That's right!
Sanji and Tony are still outside!

439
00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:40.820
Tell me... 
just who the hell are you?

440
00:28:40.820 --> 00:28:43.780
Me? I'm...

441
00:28:43.780 --> 00:28:45.740
Mr. Prince.

442
00:28:46.670 --> 00:28:51.100
I see. Mr. Prince. 
Where are you?

443
00:28:51.100 --> 00:28:53.790
'Fraid I can't say!

444
00:28:53.790 --> 00:28:56.420
If I did, you'd come get rid of me.

445
00:28:56.870 --> 00:29:00.380
Though, setting aside whether you can actually get rid of me,

446
00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:04.100
I'm not so stupid as to 
divulge information so easily.

447
00:29:04.600 --> 00:29:08.610
Unlike you, Mr. 0.

448
00:29:08.610 --> 00:29:15.060
Prince! Help! We've been caught!
There's no time!

449
00:29:15.610 --> 00:29:21.070
Come rescue me!

450
00:29:17.410 --> 00:29:21.070
Mr. Prince! Help me!

451
00:29:22.220 --> 00:29:25.570
Sounds like my crew's right by your side.

452
00:29:25.570 --> 00:29:27.820
In that case, I'm gonna–

453
00:29:32.810 --> 00:29:34.250
Troublesome bastard!

454
00:29:34.250 --> 00:29:36.020
Hello?

455
00:29:36.020 --> 00:29:39.740
We've caught him! What should
we do with this strange man?!

456
00:29:41.010 --> 00:29:43.710
Sanji... No...

457
00:29:44.470 --> 00:29:46.910
Where are you? Tell me!

458
00:29:46.910 --> 00:29:51.930
Th-The front gate of a casino
in Rainbase named Rain Dinners!

459
00:29:51.930 --> 00:29:56.610
That useless moron!
That bastard better be alive!

460
00:29:56.610 --> 00:29:59.950
Sanji!

461
00:29:59.950 --> 00:30:01.440
Our hope...

462
00:30:05.270 --> 00:30:06.700
This is great.

463
00:30:09.050 --> 00:30:11.560
Let's go to the front gate.

464
00:30:11.560 --> 00:30:15.800
Is that wise? The millions 
still don't know who their boss is.

465
00:30:15.800 --> 00:30:18.300
I won't be going as their boss.

466
00:30:18.300 --> 00:30:22.460
Aside from the number agents,
no one knows who you and I are.

467
00:30:22.460 --> 00:30:26.510
What's so strange about Crocodile,
the owner of this casino,

468
00:30:26.510 --> 00:30:31.470
going to see what has happened
in front of his building?

469
00:30:36.100 --> 00:30:37.060
Vivi!

470
00:30:40.710 --> 00:30:42.740
What are you doing, Vivi?!

471
00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:45.810
There's still time before
this room fills up with water!

472
00:30:45.810 --> 00:30:47.740
I'm going outside to get help!

473
00:30:47.740 --> 00:30:51.170
Yeah! There's no way he
kicked the bucket just now!

474
00:30:51.170 --> 00:30:53.500
If Vivi can just free him...

475
00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:56.700
And Chopper's outside too!
We might have a chance!

476
00:30:58.450 --> 00:31:00.750
Look out, Vivi!

477
00:31:04.210 --> 00:31:04.920
Vivi!

478
00:31:07.140 --> 00:31:10.260
Enough of your nonsense!

479
00:31:16.470 --> 00:31:22.100
Vivi! Wake up! Vivi!

480
00:31:17.290 --> 00:31:22.100
The gator's coming! Vivi!

481
00:31:23.790 --> 00:31:28.900
If you love your friends that much,
you can all die here together.

482
00:31:29.290 --> 00:31:32.060
The water will turn this place 
into a feeding ground

483
00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:34.870
and submerge the entire room.

484
00:31:34.870 --> 00:31:39.140
I'll drag your cheeky Mr. Prince
here too, if you'd like!

485
00:31:39.140 --> 00:31:41.000
Hopefully you 
don't mind corpses!

486
00:31:45.270 --> 00:31:48.170
Damn it!

487
00:31:57.190 --> 00:31:59.190
Oh! Owner Crocodile!

488
00:31:59.190 --> 00:32:02.160
Have you heard 
what happened in Nanohana?!

489
00:32:02.160 --> 00:32:03.740
Yes, I have.

490
00:32:03.740 --> 00:32:05.900
The whole town
—no, the whole country—

491
00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:09.530
is clamoring at the news that 
the Rebel Army and the Royal Army

492
00:32:09.530 --> 00:32:12.200
are finally about to clash!

493
00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.450
I'm not surprised.

494
00:32:13.450 --> 00:32:17.210
The king does let pirates 
attack cities freely.

495
00:32:17.210 --> 00:32:20.870
I always thought something
like this might happen.

496
00:32:20.870 --> 00:32:23.030
Hey, look! It's Sir Crocodile!

497
00:32:23.030 --> 00:32:24.960
It really is him! 
He's so wonderful!

498
00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:27.340
He rarely shows himself inside the casino!

499
00:32:29.750 --> 00:32:33.260
Sir Crocodile!

500
00:32:33.260 --> 00:32:36.220
You're as popular as ever.

501
00:32:37.890 --> 00:32:39.810
Vivi!

502
00:32:41.300 --> 00:32:44.940
Th-They've always been there....

503
00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:46.480
to help me all this time!

504
00:32:47.450 --> 00:32:51.240
I refuse to just let them die!

505
00:33:00.370 --> 00:33:02.330
Yes! She got away!

506
00:33:09.800 --> 00:33:12.240
The water's broken through the glass!

507
00:33:12.240 --> 00:33:17.800
Now we got less than 20 minutes
until this room's submerged!

508
00:33:18.750 --> 00:33:20.970
Vivi! You alright?!

509
00:33:22.310 --> 00:33:25.310
Everyone! Hang in there a little longer!

510
00:33:25.810 --> 00:33:30.770
I will bring back help!
I promise I won't abandon you!

511
00:33:30.780 --> 00:33:33.570
Yeah! We're counting on you, Vivi!

512
00:33:36.470 --> 00:33:38.350
What in the world...

513
00:33:38.350 --> 00:33:39.620
is this?

514
00:33:40.690 --> 00:33:44.680
Including the employees 
who Pell the Falcon just took out,

515
00:33:44.680 --> 00:33:48.830
it looks like all the millions
in this town have been wiped out.

516
00:33:48.830 --> 00:33:52.090
What happened?! Hey!

517
00:33:53.170 --> 00:33:55.590
A-A man named Mr. Prince...

518
00:33:56.710 --> 00:34:00.550
I thought you caught him? 
Where did he go?!

519
00:34:01.450 --> 00:34:05.200
He just now headed to
the south part of town...

520
00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:06.440
Just now?

521
00:34:06.870 --> 00:34:07.650
Him?!

522
00:34:10.090 --> 00:34:14.820
You little punk! 
Don't think you can escape me.

523
00:34:15.820 --> 00:34:17.380
Why not forget about him?

524
00:34:17.380 --> 00:34:22.080
Quiet. I've always killed everyone

525
00:34:22.080 --> 00:34:26.250
who makes a 
laughing stock out of me!

526
00:34:32.450 --> 00:34:34.450
Whoa! An earthquake?!

527
00:34:34.450 --> 00:34:37.970
This is bad! The bridge into
Rain Dinners has collapsed!

528
00:34:37.970 --> 00:34:39.230
Just out of the blue?!

529
00:34:39.230 --> 00:34:42.050
What's going on?! 
What caused it?!

530
00:34:42.660 --> 00:34:46.770
Hey! What's going on?!

531
00:34:47.510 --> 00:34:49.240
Now we can't get back to town!

532
00:34:49.240 --> 00:34:50.200
Aren't there any boats?!

533
00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:53.230
What's going on?!

534
00:34:53.780 --> 00:34:57.150
The bridge fell!

535
00:34:57.160 --> 00:35:00.160
Oh no! I can't go outside now?!

536
00:35:00.160 --> 00:35:02.730
It's not for going outside.

537
00:35:02.730 --> 00:35:06.450
It's about keeping Baroque Works
from coming back in.

538
00:35:08.030 --> 00:35:09.960
It's all part of the plan.

539
00:35:12.930 --> 00:35:17.060
Chopper's running around town
as a decoy while we speak.

540
00:35:17.060 --> 00:35:20.910
We gotta hurry. 
The rebellion's begun, too.

541
00:35:20.910 --> 00:35:23.350
Sanji!

542
00:35:25.430 --> 00:35:30.560
Think you could tell me
where they are, Princess?
